.TH NIBWARDEN\-BROWSER\-HOST 1 2026-11-08 "nibwarden" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
nibwarden\-browser\-host \- let the Bitwarden browser extension unlock with nibwarden
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B nibwarden\-browser\-host
.RI [ browser\-arguments ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
The browser starts
.B nibwarden\-browser\-host
when the official Bitwarden extension connects to the native messaging host
.BR com.8bit.bitwarden ,
in place of Bitwarden's desktop app, after
.BR "nibwarden browser enable" .
It passes the extension's messages to
.BR nibwardend (1)
and writes back its answers.
.PP
With "Unlock with biometrics" turned on in the extension, unlocking the extension asks
in nibwarden's window, every time; when nibwarden is locked, entering the master
password there unlocks both.
The extension then receives the vault's key, as it would from Bitwarden's desktop app.
nibwarden must be logged in to the same account as the extension.
.PP
It is not meant to be run by hand.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR nibwarden (1),
.BR nibwardend (1)
